# S2: P5-099: a ranged `.step` runs the points its source's simulator steps through. LTspice ends a range on
# its stop value and reads the bounds in either order (26.1.1, run); Xyce ends a grid at its last point (RG 7.10
# §2.1.36). A range whose grid ends short of its stop value is written as the list of its points where the
# target would run other points: from LTspice everywhere, on LTspice (an ascending one), Spectre and VACASK.
